        "id": 3461520
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-11T22:58:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The const eval is for generating user facing errors that we could not generate due to Overrides.\n\nThere are many transforms that we could do that would no longer follow the compile time rules of wgsl so should not generate user errors. However the results should also be valid IR (well formed).\n\nAn example might be\n\u003e var a \u003d 0.0;\n\u003e var b \u003d 1.0/a;\n \n We might choose to transform this such that we are doing divide(1.0, 0.0) in IR but we cannot fail on this and we certainly cannot forward the error to the user.",
      "parentUuid": "6b3d14f3_c4cfd3d2",
      "revId": "896a0bf3a4d59bffdf3eedc6e6828a2c6b3194c0",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "597eb0b3_b2a829c3",
