        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 358,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000257
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-11T23:21:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We will need to run this outside of substitue overrides, the spir-v reader going to IR should probably run const-eval to fold away any constants so we\u0027d want this validation to happen.\n\nIf a transform injects an invalid const construct we\u0027d also want to fail (it should never happen, and we only validation in debug for that reason). In the cases where we decide to violate the usual WGSL rules, we add capabilities so I\u0027d see us doing the same here.\n\nFor the example given, we\u0027d have to const-eval with runtime semantics given they\u0027re `var`\u0027s so it woudln\u0027t generate an error as that would const-eval.",
      "parentUuid": "8724a3e9_be78b70d",
      "revId": "896a0bf3a4d59bffdf3eedc6e6828a2c6b3194c0",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
